 "notes": "Piece construction (fortress.c) and blocks (fortress_blocks.c) are ported class by class with Java's draw order in comments; the piece tree is checked against oracle start dumps (test_structures on out/java/structures/nf-*) and the block writes against StructureBlocksProbe dumps (fo-s2a, fo-s42a). I did not run the tests or read each evidence manifest. The pending-queue drain and setRandomHeight(48,70) live in MapGenNetherBridge.Start (another file) and are ported in fortress_make_start. GPU note: pieces are calloc'd per piece and joined by pointers (struct start, pending list). Not gaps (triage 2026-09-25, out/plan/remaining-2026-09-25.md): the chest and spawner flags are read only while populating the chunk holding the target block, which already ran before any save; a rebuilt piece cannot re-place them. Formerly listed as missing: Reading a piece's saved NBT (func_143011_b: Chest, Seed, Mob) has no native counterpart; native rebuilds fortress starts from the seed, so a chest or spawner flag already set in a saved world is not restored from disk."
